## THE LANE'S SCOPE, settled by Tuesday's defaults (each one a question at the stamp: section Questions)
- **D1 WHICH sites get the code (default = every place the document prints the description of an Api line item that carries a `code` member; a closed list by PROPERTY, "at least these", any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP).** The property: an element whose text is the `description` of a package `detail[]` line, the `description` of an `optionalItems[]` row, or the `label` of a `softwareReconciliation[]` row (the Api names that label "The software line's description"), and whose Api row carries a `code`. Table THE SITES below: six sites, `L1` to `L6`, and the sites that do NOT get a code with the reason for each. Alternative (Q1): package detail lines only (`L1`, `L2`, `L5`).
- **D2 WHAT "where the Api sent one" means.** A code is printed only when it is a string whose trimmed text is not empty and not equal to the trimmed description. Absent, `null`, `""`, spaces only, or equal to the description: the line prints exactly what the unpriced document prints on main today (no placeholder, no separator, no dash: a placeholder would be a word). **The Api does send `""`** (FACT 3: `PurchaseCalculator.cs:628` sets `Code = item?.Sku ?? ""`), so the empty case is real, not theoretical. Equal to the description prints the description once (Q2). The printed code is the trimmed text of the string, as sent, never changed in case.
- **D3 THE SEPARATOR (a default, Q3): one ASCII space, the code first.** The text becomes `<quantity> <multiplication sign> <code> <description>` in the lines that join a quantity (`L1`, `L5`) and `<code> <description>` in the table cells (`L2`, `L3`, `L4`, `L6`); the suffixes `(included)` and `(credit)` stay at the end. Reason: a space adds no character that is not the data, the existing `<quantity> <multiplication sign> <description>` pattern already uses a space on each side, and any visible separator (a colon, a dash, a bracket) is a new typographic choice in a customer document. **If you find a heading, label, column head, separator word, aria-label, title or tooltip would be needed, STOP with the exact string and the site: `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <the string, where, and the site that needs it>`; never write it.**
- **D4 THE PRICED RENDER STAYS BYTE-IDENTICAL TO MAIN, and this time the proof is COMMITTED** (review follow-up 2): eight golden files captured from main's own render BEFORE any edit, compared byte for byte by a new committed test (section THE GOLDENS). The first lane proved this with uncommitted captures only; a one-character width edit to the priced short form stayed green in its committed tests.
- **D5 THE NO-PRICE CHECK MUST TELL A PART CODE FROM AN AMOUNT WITHOUT BEING WEAKER** (section THE ORACLE): a code made of digits and a dot IS read as an amount by the check as it stands (FACT 8, measured), so the check cell turns into a position-aware check; it never gets an allow-list of codes, never skips a key, never raises a threshold.
- **D6 THE TWO REVIEW FOLLOW-UPS RIDE IN THIS LANE** (section THE ORACLE, THE GOLDENS): (1) the committed oracle also reads attribute values and whole-dollar forms; (2) the no-new-word cell U10 is narrowed so a new phrase made of existing words fails, and a committed priced-markup check sees more than column heads. Each has a PLANT that the reviewer showed staying green and that must now go RED (table PLANTS). **Size: the lane stays M (FACT 10). If at 70% context you are not past Part 1, STOP at the boundary (the context band) and say so; the split Tuesday would take is Part 1 alone (tests and goldens, no source change) as one lane and Part 2 as the next: Q5.**
- **D7 NOT in this lane:** the rental documents (`RentalDocument.tsx`, `ProposalView`), a durable record of the choice (a contract member), any label change (the three words stay exactly as on main), any Api, DTO, contract, generated-client or stub change, any CSS file, `web/src/screens/ProposalPage.tsx`, any deploy, the first lane's WORD-PACK file (a records file: you do not edit it; your ADDENDUM is a new file).
- **D8 NO ARITHMETIC ON A FIGURE** (the first lane's rule, unchanged): a part code is a string; you do not parse it, compare it as a number, or format it. `web/src/test/noBrowserPricing.ts` reads money by TYPE (the generated `Decimal` members); `code` is declared `string | null` (`schema.ts:2087`), so the scanner does not read it (the file holds 0 lines naming `code` as a word: printed by program, case-insensitive); run the scanner anyway.

